Z||000000||walsh2001||10-08-2001||09:12 AM||||Recently, my GT seems to have been suffering from power loss. I have no idea where it is going, it just does not feel like the pickup is where it used to be. Any ideas? I know I can not provide much info. I know the brakes are not dragging   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I replaced the calipers. It runs kind of rough... and when I start it for the first time of the day: It turns over, and then it almost stalls before picking back up.<P>Any ideas?<P>Could old plug wires and plugs be the culprit?<P>(My Fiero also has that dreaded clicking when I step on the gas)<P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red<p>[This message has been edited by walsh2001 (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-08-2001||11:24 AM||||Change your distributor cap, rotor and plugs. Run a couple of bottles of fuel injector cleaner through also. <BR>I have no idea what is happening but this would be some of the first things I would do regardless.<BR>Good Luck!<P>Sly||||reg||1
